    "Keep pushing progressive overload on chest, back, and legs — these groups are gaining strength consistently, so continue adding small increments in load or reps each session to sustain the upward trend.",
    "Add one extra set to your shoulder work, bringing it from 4 to 5 sets per week. The shoulder strength index has stalled and volume is low relative to your pressing muscles, which can limit long-term development and joint health.",
    "Increase the load or intensity of your biceps training. The tonnage gap between biceps (432 kg) and triceps (900 kg) is significant — even with the same number of sets, aim to close that gap by using heavier weights or slowing your tempo on curls.",
    "Maintain your current recovery habits — the last period's note flagged recovery as something to watch, and this week's data shows no signs of overreaching, so your current sleep and rest approach appears to be supporting the gains well."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Strength gains on chest, back, and legs with stalled shoulders, biceps, and triceps; volume is well distributed except for underdeveloped shoulder and biceps stimulus — next period should address accessory volume while maintaining main lift progression."
}
